=== 11. Follow-up 2026-10-19: the proposed harness, ten runs

Section 10 tested the premise (slow, not hung) and section 10's prototype
booted once. This runs that prototype ten times, the same ten-run sweep as
section 2, so the numbers are comparable one for one. It is a scratch copy of
the proposed change, not a claim about the committed script: applying the two
hunks to scripts/test-atomic-install.sh is still the lead's act.

Driver (repo root; build/ is not tracked, so it is quoted here):

  OUT=build/r6/sweep2; : > "$OUT/summary.txt"
  for i in 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 08 09 10; do
    start=$(date +%s)
    bash build/r6/atomic-install-v2.sh > "$OUT/run$i.log" 2>&1
    rc=$?
    end=$(date +%s)
    boots=$(grep -c "BOOT PASS" "$OUT/run$i.log")
    fails=$(grep -c "BOOT FAIL" "$OUT/run$i.log")
    echo "run $i: rc=$rc duration=$((end-start))s boot_passes=$boots boot_fails=$fails" \
      >> "$OUT/summary.txt"
  done

